## Device integrity

`GET /integrity/challenge` hands the app a single-use challenge (valid
`INTEGRITY_CHALLENGE_MINUTES`, 5); the app has Play Integrity or App Attest
sign it into a token and sends `POST /integrity/verify` `{token, platform}`,
answered `{valid}`. Valid means the platform trusts the app and the device
**and** the token carries a fresh challenge this API issued, so a captured
verdict cannot be replayed.

- **Android:** set `GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_FILE` (a service account with the
  Play Integrity API enabled, linked in Play Console) and
  `ANDROID_PACKAGE_NAME`. Until then `/verify` answers 503.
- **iOS:** App Attest is not verified yet (503); implement
  `AppAttestVerifier.verify` in `modules/integrity/verifiers.py`, following
  Apple's "Validating apps that connect to your server".
